R = ['- **Every MRP timer\'s run-out** is resolved by its builds (`mrpdu_grade.resolve`), judged on its owner alone: the participant the testbench recorded at the expiry (below), with its opportunity derived from the posted TICKs as above ([PR #934\'s internal review](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/934#issuecomment-6938623769); [its second external review](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/934#issuecomment-6942847358)). A build\'s frames include what it left owed, which the poll sends before the next build.\n  - Only a build that can be the owner\'s settles the run-out (`mrpdu_grade.settle`, `candidate`; [its third internal review](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/934#issuecomment-6945831260)). The testbench records each build\'s participant at the build itself (`ENTRY <cycle> build_mrpdu if0 MVRP`): `srp_mbx.c`\'s `build_mrpdu` builds exactly one participant\'s MRPDU, by its slot.\n  - The builds after the run-out are taken in turn. A build recorded as another participant\'s never settles it, and neither does any build before the owner\'s opportunity.\n  - The owner\'s build settles it on the owner\'s frames of its builds (`mrpdu_grade.served`): released, or late where the owner\'s first frame comes past THE TRANSMIT\'s 49 ms after the owner\'s opportunity. With none of the owner\'s frames, it is the owner\'s own build that sends nothing: empty within 49 ms, late past it (`mrpdu_grade.anchor`).\n  - A build with no participant recorded settles the run-out only on the owner\'s frames; it is never taken for the owner\'s build that sends nothing.\n  - With no settling build within 49 ms of the owner\'s opportunity, the first build past that bound makes the run-out late. With no build after it at all, it is absent in a log that runs on past the bound (`mrpdu_grade.horizon`), and unresolved where the log ends first.\n  - Another participant\'s callback, running join timer, build or frame never defers a run-out\'s deadline, settles it or times its row.\n  - A run-out whose owner the testbench did not record at the expiry, or recorded unresolved, is `unowned` whatever its builds sent (`mrpdu_grade.resolve`, #665): it prints `STATED`, named "(owner unresolved)", and fails the run, as an unowned LeaveAll does. No other participant\'s opportunity stands in for its owner\'s. A log written before the testbench recorded owners therefore fails.\n  - A late or absent run-out is named with its owner and the owner\'s opportunity, and fails the run.\n- **A participant\'s transmit opportunity** after a timer\'s run-out is where its join timer runs out, if the timer its last commit armed still runs at the run-out: the `CTRL_LOOP_JOIN_CS`-th TICK after that commit\'s build. Otherwise it is the run-out itself. An MRPDU a timer requests goes out at that opportunity, the join timer\'s expiry (IEEE 802.1Q-2018 10.7.4.1; [#665\'s ruling of 2026-11-16](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/665#issuecomment-6930885185), Q1).\n- **Every LeaveAll timer\'s run-out has an owner** recorded at the expiry itself ([PR #934\'s review](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/934#issuecomment-6932841237)). `sim_main.cpp` reads the CPU\'s register file at the callback\'s entry: its argument is its participant\'s `timer_arg`. That argument was bound to its interface and application when the participant was created, by `observers.py` and `sim_main.cpp`\'s `note_owner`:\n  - at the `shlan_timer_init` that registered the LeaveAll timer inside `msrp_app_create` or `mvrp_app_create`;\n  - then at the interface\'s `mbx_pub_domain(index, false, ...)`, as `srp_mbx.c`\'s `create_participants` makes them.\n  - The `ENTRY` line names the owner (`ENTRY <cycle> on_la_timer if0 MSRP`), or prints `unresolved` with the argument. A `PARTICIPANT` line records each binding.\n  - Each MRPDU\'s build names its participant the same way, read off its slot at `build_mrpdu`\'s entry (`sim_main.cpp`\'s `builder_of`; slot 2n is interface n\'s MSRP, 2n + 1 its MVRP), or `unresolved` with the slot.\n- **The owner\'s LeaveAll** (`mrpdu_grade.leave_alls`) is the first of the owner\'s own MRPDUs after the run-out that declares a LeaveAll in a VectorHeader, read as lwSRP\'s `mrp_pdu.c` reads an MRPDU. Its outcome:\n  - `sent` when that MRPDU is the owner\'s first after the run-out and is committed within 49 ms of the owner\'s first transmit opportunity;\n  - `skipped` when the owner commits an MRPDU without it first;\n  - `late` past the 49 ms;\n  - `absent` with no MRPDU of the owner\'s after the run-out in a log that runs on past the bound, `unresolved` where the log ends first;\n  - `unowned` where the expiry has no owner recorded, or its owner recorded unresolved. It is never bound to whichever participant\'s LeaveAll comes first.\n  - A skipped, late, absent or unowned LeaveAll prints `STATED`, named, and fails the run. The `JOINS` line counts them, and the LeaveAll\'s row is timed on the owner\'s LeaveAll, from the owner\'s first transmit opportunity.\n- **What this proves**, in a log the harness passes:\n  - each LeaveAll timer\'s expiry has an owner the testbench recorded at the expiry;\n  - where the log runs on past that owner\'s first transmit opportunity and the bound, the owner\'s next committed MRPDU carries the LeaveAll;\n  - and it is committed within 49 ms of the owner\'s first transmit opportunity, as the harness derives it from the owner\'s commits and the TICKs.\n  - An expiry the log ends before is counted `unresolved` and proves nothing. A participant created otherwise than as one MSRP and one MVRP before its interface\'s Domain is published is left unbound, so its expiries are `unowned`.\n  - It holds at commit, not on the wire, which `T_egress` covers.\n  - For every MRP timer\'s run-out, a join, periodic or LeaveAll timer\'s: the testbench recorded its owner at the expiry; and against the owner\'s first transmit opportunity, the first build that can be the owner\'s after it, recorded as the owner\'s or with no participant recorded, at or after the opportunity, settles it within 49 ms of it: the owner\'s first frame committed within 49 ms, or the owner\'s own build that sends nothing run within 49 ms. Where no build can settle it and the log ends within 49 ms of the opportunity, it is unresolved; otherwise the run fails, late or absent.\n- **Each group\'s shortest and longest**, and its run-outs by outcome, print on a `JOINS` line. An interval under 181.0 ms or over 239.0 ms, Table 4.3\'s 180.0 to 240.0 ms less `T_egress` at each end since the harness sees commits (the egress ruling\'s item 1), or a late, absent or unowned run-out, prints `STATED` and fails the run whatever findings it records.\n[`egress_ledger.py`](egress_ledger.py) holds the rows the egress decides to their ledger ([#894\'s held-egress ruling](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/894#issuecomment-6871343905), item (a)).\n`backlog-owed`\'s seven rows are set by the scenario\'s 60 ms egress hold, which no CPU lever moves: they miss their budget at every point, and a run with `--record-budget-findings` records every miss and fails none.\n[FR_NFR.md 3.4.1](../../../docs/reference/FR_NFR.md#341-control-service-budget-and-normative-timing) charges TX backpressure to the service budget, so they stay recorded misses, not passes, and a new or larger miss fails the leg.\n- **The ledger** (`LEDGER`) is derived at 8x8/1if, the one point that has one, by #894\'s round-6 ruling: each figure is the scenario\'s egress hold (`HOLD_MS`, read from `scenario.py`\'s `backlog-owed` group) plus the service behind it at its measurement (`MEASURED`, the larger of the merged image\'s and the composed image\'s, `MERGED` and `COMPOSED`, by [#894\'s ruling of 2026-11-16](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/894#issuecomment-6914952893) on the composition with #901, item 1) plus 5 %, rounded up to 0.01 ms (`figure`). [Section 13](../../../docs/design/SPLIT_CONTROL_MEMORY.md#the-shapes-and-8x81if)\'s table states both measurements and the figures; the self-test holds the table to the tool, row for row and figure for figure, and the derivation to the rule, computed apart.\n- **A larger miss.** A measured instance of a ledger row over its figure fails, by as little as one cycle of the bus, whatever its name; so does one never released or answered, whose time is a lower bound.\n- **A new miss.** A budget miss of any other row fails, and so do a ledger row with no measured instance and any instance not measured.\n- **Its inputs** are the harness\'s own: a results directory\'s group grades, whose figures are exact to 10 ns, beside its run\'s `results.json`, whose refusals fail (a group the harness refused has no grade of its own), or a run\'s log, whose `BUDGET` lines name every instance over its budget to 1 us. A row read from a log is held at the most its printed figure can be, so one printed at its ledger figure fails, and a log must end in its run\'s summary, with no refusal and one `BUDGET` line a budget miss.\n- `egress_ledger.py --selftest` runs its controls in its own process and as a process of their own, whose exit status is the verdict. The unchanged ledger passes, and each row one cycle over its figure, and 36.76 ms over, exits 1 naming it. It refuses fourteen mutants, among them one that waives a ledger row by its name whatever its size, one that reads no run\'s refusals, a figure with no 5 % on its service, the 5 % taken on the hold too, a hold not the scenario\'s, and a figure at the merged image\'s measurement where the composed one is larger.\n\n', "[`mrpdu_grade.py`](mrpdu_grade.py) adds a row to every group that holds its load: each MRPDU a join, periodic or LeaveAll timer owes, against THE TRANSMIT's bound, `CTRL_LOOP_TX_BOUND_MS` as `ctrl_loop.h` derives it (`mrpdu_grade.BUDGET_MS`, never typed; [#894's round 2 ruling](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/894#issuecomment-6871343905), item (b)(i)), where it held it to T_svc before. The row runs from its owner's transmit opportunity to the commit of the owner's frames of the builds after the run-out; another participant's frame in the same builds, or in the same commit, neither times nor ends it. The opportunity is the TICK that ran the timer out, or, where the owner's join timer still runs then, the TICK that runs that out ([#665's ruling of 2026-11-16](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/665#issuecomment-6930885185), Q1: a protocol-mandated wait is not CPU service time; the bound is unchanged). A timer that ends with nothing to send has a build that sends no frame, and no row. The self-test holds a row at the bound within it and one 1 ms over it a miss.\n"]
